description:
In repos/relevance-sink-vessel/src/index.ts, the GET /health handler must verify the SurrealDB dependency instead of reporting ok unconditionally (a miswired deployment currently passes every automatic health check while all writes fail; proven 2026-09-15, validation/reports/wiring-green-vs-miswired-proof). Find this exact anchor text:

```ts
      if (req.method === "GET" && url.pathname === "/health") {
        return Response.json({ status: "ok", vessel: "relevance-sink-vessel" });
      }
```

and replace it with exactly:

```ts
      if (req.method === "GET" && url.pathname === "/health") {
        // Health means "my one dependency answers", not "my process runs" —
        // an unconditional ok reported a vessel healthy while every write
        // failed ConnectionRefused (2026-09-15 wiring proof).
        try {
          const probe = await fetch(`${SURREALDB_URL}/sql`, {
            method: "POST",
            headers: {
              "Accept": "application/json",
              "Content-Type": "text/plain",
              "surreal-ns": SURREALDB_NAMESPACE,
              "surreal-db": SURREALDB_DATABASE,
              "Authorization": basicAuth(SURREALDB_USERNAME, SURREALDB_PASSWORD),
            },
            body: "RETURN 1;",
            signal: AbortSignal.timeout(2000),
          });
          if (!probe.ok) throw new Error(`store probe ${probe.status}`);
          return Response.json({ status: "ok", vessel: "relevance-sink-vessel" });
        } catch {
          return Response.json(
            { status: "degraded", vessel: "relevance-sink-vessel", store: "unreachable" },
            { status: 503 },
          );
        }
      }
```

